        "original_id": "9ead8824-3b94-5a59-a47e-31b73f2c8aa2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Birmingham City F.C., Aston Villa, Norwich City\n- People: Steve Bruce\n- Events: 2005–06 Birmingham City F.C. season\n- Roles: football manager, player\n- Topics: English football league system, Premier League, Championship, Football League Cup\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Bruce was born on 31 December 1960 and is an English professional football manager and former player.\n- Steve Bruce was offered an apprenticeship and played more than 200 games for the club before joining Norwich City in 1984.\n- Norwich City won the Football League Cup in 1985 with Steve Bruce at the club.\n- The 2005–06 season was Birmingham City F.C.'s 103rd season in the English football league system and their fourth season in the Premier League.\n- Birmingham City F.C. were managed by Steve Bruce during the 2005–06 season.\n- Birmingham City F.C. finished 18th in the 20-team Premier League in 2005–06 and were relegated to the Championship for 2006–07.\n- Steve Bruce is currently the manager of Aston Villa.",
